p2u: 1
deck:
  title: Urban Events
  subtitle: Ticketing for Pakistan — publish, sell in PKR, scan at the gate
  author: Urban Events
  theme: white
slides:
  - id: title
    layout: title
    title: Urban Events
    body: Every great event starts here — ticketing built for Pakistan.
    notes: >
      Urban Events (urbanevents.pk) is an event ticketing platform for Pakistan:
      publish an event page, sell tickets in PKR, check guests in from any phone.
      Pitch goal: seed interest from investors and early organizer partners.

  - id: problem
    layout: content
    title: The problem
    body: |
      Event ticketing in Pakistan still runs on paper and cash: queue at the gate,
      fake tickets, no data. Organizers juggle bank transfers and spreadsheets;
      attendees have no trusted way to buy ahead.
    notes: >
      Pain points: cash queues at the gate, scalpers and fake tickets, no trust
      between attendee and organizer, and zero sales data. (Framing based on the
      market the site targets — student societies, MUNs, meetups.)

  - id: solution
    layout: content
    title: The solution
    body: |
      A self-serve platform: publish a branded event page, sell tickets in PKR
      through JazzCash, Easypaisa and bank transfer, and scan QR codes at the
      gate from any phone. Free for free events.
    notes: >
      Direct from urbanevents.pk: event pages, PKR checkout with local gateways,
      QR check-in, live analytics, custom branding, attendee messaging, CSV
      exports, automated payouts.

  - id: how-it-works
    layout: diagram
    title: How it works
    blocks:
      - kind: diagram
        source: |
          direction: right
          fan: Attendee
          browse: Browse event page
          pay: Pay in PKR
          ticket: QR ticket
          gate: Scan at gate
          dash: Organizer dashboard
          fan -> browse -> pay -> ticket -> gate
          gate -> dash: live counts
    notes: >
      One flow, end to end: attendee browses, pays in PKR, receives a QR ticket,
      gets scanned at the gate, and the organizer dashboard syncs live counts.

  - id: market
    layout: metric-row
    title: Market (estimates)
    blocks:
      - kind: metric
        label: Target events / year
        value: 50k+
      - kind: metric
        label: Avg paid tickets / event
        value: 150
      - kind: metric
        label: Addressable GMV / yr
        value: $15M+
    notes: >
      ASSUMPTIONS, not verified figures: tens of thousands of MUNs, concerts,
      workshops, sports weeks and charity drives run yearly across Pakistan;
      ~150 paid tickets per event at ~PKR 1,000 average implies a multi-million
      dollar ticket GMV pool for a 5% fee to address.

  - id: model
    layout: content
    title: Business model
    body: |
      Free for free events; a simple **5% per paid ticket** added at checkout —
      no monthly fees, no contracts. At scale: organizer SaaS for branding,
      messaging and analytics.
    notes: >
      Verified from the site's pricing: 5% per paid ticket, free for free events,
      no monthly fees. Fee math: on a PKR 1,000 ticket we keep $1000 \times 5\% = 50$ PKR;
      an event of 300 tickets yields $300 \times 50 = 15{,}000$ PKR.

  - id: traction
    layout: timeline
    title: Traction & roadmap (assumptions)
    blocks:
      - kind: markdown
        body: |
          - **Now** — live product: pages, PKR checkout, QR check-in
          - **Next** — 100 organizer signups, first paid-event cohort
          - **Later** — seat maps, season passes, organizer SaaS tier
    notes: >
      ASSUMPTIONS: the public site does not disclose traction numbers. Roadmap
      is our proposal — validate current volumes with the founders before
      investing.

  - id: why-now
    layout: content
    title: Why now
    body: |
      Local rails (JazzCash, Easypaisa) are mainstream, QR adoption is ubiquitous,
      and student-run events are already digital-first. No incumbent owns
      self-serve ticketing for Pakistan.
    notes: >
      The enablers: instant local payment rails, phones-as-scanners, and a young
      organizer base. Positioning claim — verify competitive landscape.

  - id: team
    layout: content
    title: Team
    body: |
      Placeholder — founders with product and payments experience in Pakistan.
      *Replace with real bios before presenting.*
    notes: >
      PLACEHOLDER: no team info on the public site. Fill in founder names,
      backgrounds and advisors before any investor meeting.

  - id: ask
    layout: content
    title: The ask
    body: |
      Seeking pilot organizers and a pre-seed round to grow GTM. One line of code,
      one event page, one gate — come sell out your next event with us.
    notes: >
      CTA: partner pilots with student societies and MUN organizers now; open a
      pre-seed conversation. Contact via urbanevents.pk.

  - id: end
    layout: end
    title: Thank you
    body: urbanevents.pk — every great event starts here.
    notes: >
      Close: invite questions; offer a live demo of publish → sell → scan.
